# Strict IRAuth hardware allow-list, one lowercase USB interface selector per line.
#
# Format: VID:PID@IFACE, where IFACE is the USB bInterfaceNumber for the exact
# UVC interface that exposes the verified IR/depth stream. Matching only a
# VID:PID is deliberately not accepted because many laptop camera modules expose
# both RGB and IR interfaces under the same USB device ID.
#
# Leave this file empty unless the exact interface has been verified to expose
# an IR/depth stream on Linux. IRAuth also accepts video nodes whose
# kernel-visible name explicitly contains IR/infrared/depth.
#
# Example format only (NOT an approved device):
# 1234:abcd@02
